t organises delivery around four industry practices - Banking & Financial Services, Logistics and Transportation, Digital Commerce, and Emerging Verticals (Telecom, Hi-Tech and Utilities) - selling to banks, fintechs, carriers, third-party logistics providers, ports and terminals, shippers, logistics …","certs":"","co":"SAKSOFT LIMITED","depth":"deep","end_markets":"Banking & Financial Services - banks, cards and payments, wealth and capital management, regtech, credit bureau, fintechs|Logistics and Transportation - third-party logistics, freight carriers, ports and terminals, shippers, retail and commerce logistics, logistics ISVs|Digital Commerce - B2C/B2B/D2C commerce, digital commerce operations, digital experience platforms, commercial ISVs and product companies|Emerging Verticals - Telecom, Hi-Tech and Utilities|India operations across five locations (Chennai, Noida, Bengaluru, Mumbai, Pune); clients in six Indian states and ten international …","expansion":"Saksoft is asset-light and discloses no manufacturing capacity: the BRSR states 'As Saksoft is an IT Services Company, we do not have any Manufacturing plants', with plants shown as Not Applicable and five national offices. Expansion is therefore framed as capability, footprint and platform build-out rather than plant capex. The Board's Report describes investments in a transition 'from people-dependent processes to an AI-driven innovation model', with heavy investment in new AI skill sets and capability frameworks; R&D costs are described as integrated into the operational fabric rather than …","grades":{"rel":0,"s":"","wm90":null},"industry":"IT - Software","isin":"INE667G01023","kpi":null,"listed_on":"","litigation":{"as_of":"","material":true,"note":"The routed 'RELATED-PARTY TRANSACTIONS' block actually opens with Standalone Note 22(a) Contingent Liabilities, which discloses income-tax matters and states that 'the future cash outflows on items above are determinable only on receipt of the decision or judgment that is pending at various forums and authorities' - i.e. tax proceedings are pending against the Company at multiple forums. The Company adds that it 'does not expect the outcome of these proceedings to have an adverse material effect on the financial results'. No auditor's report, CARO annexure or regulatory-order disclosure is routed to this bundle, so this is the only litigation evidence available here; the flag records that disclosed pending proceedings exist, not that they were assessed material by management."},"mdna":"Management expects the rapid adoption of Artificial Intelligence, cloud technologies and data-driven operating models to continue reshaping enterprise technology investments in FY 2026-27|As organisations move from experimentation to enterprise-wide AI deployment, demand is expected to increase for trusted partners capable of delivering secure, scalable and outcome-driven transformation|Enterprises are balancing two priorities simultaneously - remaining competitive in an AI-led market while optimising ongoing technology spend - which is driving vendor consolidation and centralised, AI-enabled …","objects":null,"oem":"","one_liner":"Domain-led digital transformation services provider that innovates, modernises, optimises and sustains enterprise IT ecosystems for banking & financial services, logistics, digital commerce and emerging-vertical clients, largely outside India.","peer_panel":{"asof":"2026-08-14","industry":"IT - Software","peers":[{"ebitda_margin":18.4,"fy":"FY26","growth_basis":"7y CAGR","mcap":1792,"name":"Silver Touch Technologies Ltd","pat":35.7,"pat_growth":19.0,"pe":50.2,"rev":345.6,"rev_growth":7.3,"s":"SILVERTUC","source":"drhp","why":"named in DRHP"},{"ebitda_margin":7.9,"fy":"FY26","growth_basis":"7y CAGR","mcap":1699,"name":"Sasken Technologies Ltd","pat":58.6,"pat_growth":-6.0,"pe":29.0,"rev":1113.2,"rev_growth":12.0,"s":"SASKEN","source":"drhp","why":"named in DRHP"},{"ebitda_margin":21.9,"fy":"FY26","growth_basi