ing\"], \"Digital Commerce\": [\"Helsinki\", \"Oslo\", \"Vue Storefront\", \"Salesforce Commerce Starter Store\", \"API and Integration Suite\", \"Unite\", \"VoiceBOT\", \"Commerce Command Centre Framework\"]}","promises":[],"promises_total":0,"promoters":[{"name":"Mr. Aditya Krishna (DIN: 00031345)","role":"Promoter / Executive Director; Chairman & Managing Director - the Corporate Governance Report states the Board 'is chaired by an Executive Promoter Director', and he is listed as CMD among Key Managerial Personnel in the related-party note"}],"related":"[{\"name\": \"Sak Industries Private Limited and its subsidiaries\", \"relation\": \"related party\", \"note\": \"Disclosed as the enterprise which has significant influence over the Company\"}, {\"name\": \"Saksoft Inc, USA\", \"relation\": \"subsidiary\", \"note\": \"Subsidiary / step-down subsidiary named in the …","risks":[{"note":"Ranked first in the BRSR material-issues table: external attacks, malware, compromised credentials and business email compromise via phishing may result in data loss and loss of reputation. Mitigated through a mature Information Security Management System, defence-in-depth control architecture, multi-factor authentication, an enhanced data-leakage-prevention platform, encryption and backup/recovery, with ISO 27001 certification and SOC 2 Type II attestations cited as reinforcement. Financial implication flagged negative.","risk":"Cyber security incidents"},{"note":"Unauthorised use or disclosure of employee, company or customer data may lead to breach of customer contracts, regulator fines or penalties and reputational damage - a structural exposure for a services firm operating inside client BFS and commerce systems. Mitigation is access control, need-to-know provisioning and regular access reviews. Financial implication flagged negative.","risk":"Data privacy"},{"note":"The Company states it 'operates in the global environment and has maximum business from US geography, hence currency fluctuation is a major risk'. It follows a consistent hedging policy covering most of the net exposure in USD, GBP and Euro, hedged only in India and never beyond 12 months, with gains/losses booked in the revenue line - so a sustained move beyond the 12-month hedge horizon is unhedged. Financial implication flagged negative.","risk":"Foreign exchange exposure with concentration in the US geography"},{"note":"A changing geopolitical landscape in multiple regions (war scenarios) and macroeconomic uncertainty around interest-rate cuts may compress customer discretionary technology spend and reduce opportunities. Mitigation is limited to monitoring and reporting geopolitical risk to the Board's Risk Management Committee. Financial implication flagged negative.","risk":"Geopolitical and macroeconomic conditions"},{"note":"The Company states the risk of attrition 'may hamper long-term sustainability' - the core structural risk of a people-based delivery model. Mitigation is retention and recognition through loyalty and performance award schemes. Financial implication flagged negative.","risk":"Talent demand and employee attrition"},{"note":"Non-compliance with anti-corruption laws or unethical practices may lead to regulatory penalties, reputational damage and loss of stakeholder trust; separately, the absence of effective reporting mechanisms could leave unethical practices unreported and lead to governance failures. Mitigated through a zero-tolerance Anti-Bribery and Anti-Corruption Policy, a Code of Conduct with structured training and participation tracking, a Supplier Risk Assessment Checklist for third-party due diligence, and a confidential whistleblower channel with non-retaliation protection.","risk":"Business ethics, anti-corruption and whistleblower governance"},{"note":"Well-being (physical, mental and emotional) across employees and the extended workforce is treated as a material issue, with force-majeure events such as medical emergencies and weather-related disruption specifically named. Occupational health and safety practices are stated to be aligned with ISO 45001:2018.","risk":"Employee well-being and workplace safety"},{"note":"Treated as both risk and opportunity: reducing GHG emissions while building resilience to evolving climate conditions, addressed through renewable energy, energy-efficient lighting, sustainable transportation and buildings, and a near-term target set with SBTi.","risk":"Climate action and energy management"}],"rpt":{},"rpt_date":"","s":"SAKSOFT","sector":"Information Technology","sk":{"as_of":"2026-06-17","cagrs":[{"cagr":"3.7%","period":"CY2024-CY2029P","segment":"Global M&E market"},{"cagr":"4.5%","period":"CY2024-CY2029P","segment":"Broadcasting & streaming (incl. advertising)"},{"cagr":"~10%","period":"CY2024-CY2029P","segment":"OTT (on-demand + FAST)"},{"cagr":"9.8%","period":"CY2024-CY2029P","segment":"Global on-demand OTT"},{"cagr":"15.1%","period":"CY2024-CY2029P","segment":"Linear OTT (FAST)"},{"cagr":"~8.4%","period":"CY2024-CY2029P","segment":"Global cloud broadcasting software SAM"}],"drivers":"Technological disruption from automation, AI and digital transformation rendering traditional skills insufficient|Growing demand for upskilling and reskilling across a multi-generational workforce|Talent shortages and widening skill gaps between job requirements and available skills|Shift to …","industry":"IT - Software","market_size":[{"metric":"Global M&E market","value":"Rs 251.1 trillion (US$3.0 trillion)","year":"CY2024"},{"metric":"Global M&E market (projected)","value":"Rs 301.3 trillion (US$3.6 trillion)","year":"CY2029P"},{"metric":"Broadcasting & streaming share of M&E","value":"~16.6%","year":"CY2024"},{"metric":"Global on-demand OTT (SVOD/AVOD/TVOD)","value":"Rs 17.7 trillion (US$211.1 billion)","year":"CY2024"},{"metric":"Global on-demand OTT (projected)","value":"Rs 28.2 trillion (US$336.6 billion)","year":"CY2029P"},{"metric":"Linear OTT (FAST) revenue","value":"Rs 